Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: simple: restore IPU4 links after external use

An independent CameraManager can change the shared media graph while the
persistent desktop CameraManager is idle. setupLinks() currently skips
ioctls based on its local flags. After native rear capture, desktop front
startup left both CSI inputs enabled on the same BE sink and failed with
EPIPE before opening a firmware stream.

For the existing intel-ipu6/ipu4p idle-device path, program mutable links
according to the requested pipeline even when cached enabled flags agree.
MediaLink::setEnabled() issues the ioctl and updates its flags only after
success; the kernel handles already matching state. Preserve immutable
links, routing boundaries, error propagation and other devices' behavior.
No retry, delay, device reset or public ABI change is introduced.

---
diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -705,6 +705,8 @@
 int SimpleCameraData::setupLinks()
 {
 	int ret;
+	/* Another CameraManager can change links while our camera is idle. */
+	const bool restoreLinks = pipe()->releaseIdleVideo();
 
 	/*
 	 * Configure all links along the pipeline. Some entities may not allow
@@ -739,7 +741,7 @@
 				if (link == sinkLink)
 					continue;
 
-				if ((link->flags() & MEDIA_LNK_FL_ENABLED) &&
+				if ((restoreLinks || (link->flags() & MEDIA_LNK_FL_ENABLED)) &&
 				    !(link->flags() & MEDIA_LNK_FL_IMMUTABLE)) {
 					ret = link->setEnabled(false);
 					if (ret < 0)
@@ -748,7 +750,8 @@
 			}
 		}
 
-		if (!(sinkLink->flags() & MEDIA_LNK_FL_ENABLED)) {
+		if ((restoreLinks && !(sinkLink->flags() & MEDIA_LNK_FL_IMMUTABLE)) ||
+		    !(sinkLink->flags() & MEDIA_LNK_FL_ENABLED)) {
 			ret = sinkLink->setEnabled(true);
 			if (ret < 0)
 				return ret;
